{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_00-04-05-etcd_raft-real-run; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nupd={\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The contrast recorded from source last turn has an empirical half that a small probe can settle, so I filed it rather than leaving it as reading: the same message type reaches the same follower path with a legal term and with no term at all, and in the second case the follower adopts the sender as its leader. The harness now emits a setup event so the legal heartbeat can be compared as a control and the term-less heartbeat as the observation. The question asks how far the term-zero trust goes for a network type; the interpretation will treat the observation as a bound on the classification finding rather than as a second defect, because the term-less form is an illegal field that no correct peer produces.\\\",\n \\\"investigations\\\":[{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@term_zero_network_path\\\",\n  \\\"parent_id\\\":\\\"ce33f7b508af4244883ac9c81a2a4696-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"question\\\":\\\"Does a message of a type that legitimately travels the network reach the same follower path when it carries no term field at all, as the classification finding implies, and what does that say about the boundary between the classification gap and ordinary unauthenticated input?\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src_step_local\\\",\\\"src_stepfollower_leadset\\\",\\\"src_islocal\\\",\\\"src_rawstep\\\"],\n  \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"Step skips every term comparison for a message whose term is zero and dispatches on type, so a MsgHeartbeat with no term field from any peer reaches stepFollower, which zeroes the election timer and adopts m.From as leader even though the follower already had a live leader; unlike the missing MsgForgetLeader classification, this needs an illegal field, so it bounds the finding rather than duplicating it.\\\",\n  \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Deliver a real leader heartbeat from node 1 to follower 2 (control: lead becomes 1) and then the same message type from node 3 with no term field, sampling the follower's reported leader after each: a lead of 3 from the second delivery shows the term-zero path acts, and the absence of a step error shows it is accepted rather than rejected.\\\"}],\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@term_zero_network_path\\\",\n  \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src_step_local\\\",\\\"src_stepfollower_leadset\\\",\\\"src_islocal\\\",\\\"src_rawstep\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Ninth test function: a real election among three equal-log voters, then one real heartbeat from the leader to follower 2 (control), then the same message type from node 3 with no term field, emitting the follower's state and reported leader around each delivery.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"A peer may deliver a protobuf message of any type to the documented inbound path, including one whose optional term field is left unset.\\\",\n    \\\"The delivery helper writes each Ready's HardState and Entries to the node's storage before Advance.\\\",\n    \\\"Voters are {1,2,3} from equal snapshots at index=10/term=1 with CheckQuorum+PreVote; the follower has heard from the leader, so its election timer is fresh and its leader context is live.\\\"],\n   \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"ReadOnlyLeaseBased configurations.\\\",\\\"Any claim that a correct peer would send a term-less network message; the probe deliberately uses an illegal field to test the boundary.\\\"],\n   \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"election_tick\\\":10,\\\"heartbeat_tick\\\":1,\\\"voters\\\":[1,2,3]}},\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Elect node 1 for real, emit follower 2's state before anything is delivered, deliver node 1's real heartbeat and emit the follower's reported leader, then deliver a MsgHeartbeat with the same fields but from node 3 and with no term field, emitting the returned error and the follower's reported leader again.\\\",\n  \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"The raft module owns which messages it accepts from the network and owns the reading of a message whose term field is unset.\\\",\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"t_setup\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"t_setup\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"value\\\":2}]}],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"t_control_heartbeat\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"node\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"t_setup\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"lead_after\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: a legal heartbeat from the leader sets the follower's reported leader to 1.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"t_term0_heartbeat\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"node\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"t_setup\\\",\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"term\\\",\\\"value\\\":0}],\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"lead_after\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\\\"description\\\":\\\"Boundary: a message with no term field must not change the follower's leader context; a witness with lead_after=3 is the violated case, showing the term-zero path acts for a network type as well.\\\"}]}}\njson.dump(upd,open('draft/update.json','w'),indent=1,ensure_ascii=False)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_00-04-05-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
