{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Grounding the contrast recorded from source last turn: registered child question @term_zero_network_path and filed a ninth test function that delivers one real heartbeat from the leader to follower 2 (control, lead becomes 1) and then the same message type from node 3 with no term field at all, sampling the returned error and the follower's reported leader after each. The harness now emits a setup event so the control is comparable under the same admission, and the two comparisons are the control (legal heartbeat sets lead to 1, expected holds) and the boundary observation (a term-less network message must not change the leader context, with a witness of lead_after=3 as the violated case). The local run shows exactly that: the real heartbeat moved the reported leader to 1, and the term-less heartbeat was accepted with no error and moved it to 3. The question and experiment are framed so the result bounds the classification finding rather than duplicating it, since the term-less form is an illegal field no correct peer produces; validation passed with the execution requested and the receipt plus interpretation are pending.\"}"}}
